# .gitattributes
#
# GL-LOADER (TODO.md, GODS_LAWS.md L-07 EXCECAO No 1, L-27, L-40).
#
# THE FACT this file exists to fix: the Windows CI job's configure
# step failed at src/render/CMakeLists.txt's sha256 gate -
# third_party/khronos/gl.xml measured as
# d76ff1730ba90801a0c901fa38f643fcd1ad9da475a9c5a8344010be41c30687
# instead of the recorded
# fba2eaa6262cededdba0dd3cd1e3b1806c24899a7c5df8158467e41c19969426.
#
# THE PROOF, not an assumption: recomputing sha256 of the committed
# (LF) blob with every "\n" replaced by "\r\n" reproduces the CI's
# reported value byte for byte. Nothing else about the file's content
# differs between platforms - only line-ending conversion explains the
# mismatch. This is git's own default behavior on the windows-latest
# runner (no .gitattributes existed before this file, so git fell back
# to its own text auto-detection + the runner's default line-ending
# conversion), not a defect in gl_registry_codegen, in CMake's
# file(SHA256 ...), or in the value recorded in this directory's own
# README.md.
#
# WHY THIS MATTERS BEYOND ONE CI RUN: EXCECAO No 1's obligation 3
# (GODS_LAWS.md L-07) is a textual promise - "O arquivo entra
# verbatim, byte a byte, e nao se modifica" - that git's default
# checkout behavior does not keep on Windows without an explicit
# override. The sha256 gate below did exactly its job (GODS_LAWS.md
# L-40: it counted, compared against a real expectation, and refused
# to pass silently); the fix belongs here, in how git hands the file
# to the gate, not in the gate itself.
#
# "binary" is shorthand for "-diff -merge -text": disables line-ending
# conversion on checkout AND on checkin, on every platform equally;
# disables line-based diff (a byte-identical vendored file should
# never be diffed as text - "Binary files differ" is the honest
# report for a file this law forbids editing); disables line-based
# merge for the same reason. This is a NO-OP on every Linux CI job
# (ubuntu-latest, all five fedora:44-based jobs, and every other
# platform this project targets outside CI): those checkouts already
# receive the file exactly as committed (LF), because Linux git does
# not convert line endings by default. Only the windows-latest
# runner's behavior changes - which is the one platform where the
# mismatch was ever observed.
#
# SCOPE, deliberately narrow: this covers the two files EXCECAO No 1
# actually vendors under third_party/khronos/ - the registry itself
# and the upstream license text obligation 1 requires to travel with
# it (see that directory's own README.md). It does NOT use a
# third_party/khronos/** glob, because that directory also holds
# README.md, which is OUR OWN prose (AGPL-3.0-or-later,
# GODS_LAWS.md L-21) - a normal file meant to stay diffable as text.
# A blanket glob would have silently made it binary too, for zero
# benefit.
#
# THE INVERSE, checked before this file was written: no other tracked
# file in this repository has a hash, checksum, or other byte-exact
# comparison against its own committed content (verified by
# enumerating every "sha256"/"md5"/"checksum"/"file(SHA" occurrence in
# the repository - third_party/khronos/gl.xml's gate in
# src/render/CMakeLists.txt is the only one). The two files this
# .gitattributes protects are therefore the entire set that needed
# protecting; no other pattern was left out.
#
# This file adds NO behavior for text/diff-comparing gates elsewhere
# in the tree (tests/tools/check_dup_laws.sh's byte-for-byte DUP-BLOCK
# comparison between GODS_LAWS.md and ESCOPO.md, gitleaks's history
# scan, or any tests/tools/*.sh gate) - none of them match the two
# paths below, and none of the Linux shells (bash/dash/zsh across the
# five container images) that run those gates change behavior from
# this file's presence, since Linux checkouts of the two paths below
# were already byte-identical to what they are now.

third_party/khronos/gl.xml binary
third_party/khronos/LICENSE-APACHE-2.0.txt binary
